  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "so Two things that are already \"Buggy\" with the new Client Release, \n\n1: Default Mic is NO LONGER handled through the VRC Client anymore, But Directly through your computer's Sound Properties; whatever your \"Default Mic\" is set to.... which is really annoying, especially when you have different devices to switch between, you also have to re-launch the client after changing the default mic to get it to work, Please fix this!\n\n2: for some reason now with my Playspace Mover; i don't have my Full body tracking turned on, but a single Tracker Ball gets Emulated by VRChat, so every time i change an avatar, VRChat automatically assumes i have my full body tracking on, and throws me into the Calibration mode, and will automatically bypass my \"Sitting/Standing\" play mode, and force my avatar to crouch..... Like  i'm sitting down (which I am doing seated play) but in order to fix it i have to adjust myself with the playspace mover, and if i accidentally \"Bump\" the reset, it throws me back into crouch! \nPlease fix this!",
